{"memo": "NVIDIA CORP (NVDA) delivered a robust finish to its fiscal year 2025, posting revenue of roughly $73 billion, a net profit of about $30 billion, EPS of $11.00 and operating cash flow near $38 billion. The fiscal‑year‑2025 results reflect a 45 % compound annual growth rate in revenue from FY2023 ($26.9 billion) and a sharp acceleration in profitability, with net margins hovering around 41 % versus 45 % in FY2023. FY2024 served as the bridge, delivering $50.1 billion in sales, $20 billion of net income, EPS of $7.50 and $25 billion of operating cash flow, while preserving strong gross margins near 60 %.

The company’s margin profile has improved steadily: gross margin rose from ~55 % in FY2023 to ~65 % in FY2025, underscoring the leverage of its data‑center and AI chip ecosystem. EPS growth mirrors revenue expansion, climbing from $4.50 in FY2023 to $11.00 in FY2025. Cash generation has remained ample, supporting continued share repurchases and R&D investment, with free cash flow exceeding $30 billion in FY2025.

Overall, NVIDIA’s fiscal‑year trajectory showcases a high‑growth, high‑margin business expanding its leadership in AI and graphics, with consistent earnings acceleration and robust cash flow. One‑line view: NVDA remains a premier growth play, though its valuation now reflects much of its recent AI‑driven expansion."}
